//! # Sovereign Engine Security Policy
//!
//! ## Invariant: State-Resident Rearm Authority
//!
//! The `rearm()` operation is the only authorized transition from a terminal
//! engine state (`Sealed` or `SafeState`) to the active `Idle` operational state.
//!
//! ### Formulating Principle
//!
//! **Persistence does not restore authority.**
//!
//! Persistence presents evidence. The resident engine state independently proves
//! whether that evidence belongs to the exact terminal state currently held by
//! the engine.
//!
//! A `PersistenceReceipt` is therefore not itself authority to reset the engine.
//! It is cryptographic evidence whose validity is determined by recomputation
//! against the engine's resident terminal lineage.
//!
//! ### Mathematical Authorization Rule
//!
//! The transition $S_{\text{terminal}} \to S_{\text{idle}}$ is authorized **if and only if**:
//!
//! ```text
//!               +-------------------------------------------------------+
//!   rearm() <=> | C_receipt == H( VERSION                               |
//!               |               || DOMAIN_PERSISTENCE_RECEIPT           |
//!               |               || H_terminal                           |
//!               |               || Encode_Canonical(artifact) )         |
//!               +-------------------------------------------------------+
//! ```
//!
//! More precisely, the commitment supplied by the receipt **MUST NOT** be trusted
//! directly. The engine independently computes:
//!
//! ```text
//! C_expected = H(
//!     VERSION
//!     || DOMAIN_PERSISTENCE_RECEIPT
//!     || H_terminal
//!     || Encode_Canonical(artifact)
//! )
//! ```
//!
//! and authorizes rearm **only** when:
//!
//! ```text
//! C_receipt == C_expected
//! ```
//!
//! ### Canonical Artifact Encoding
//!
//! `Encode_Canonical(artifact)` is the unique, deterministic binary framing:
//!
//! ```text
//! u64_le(artifact.len()) || artifact_bytes
//! ```
//!
//! No alternate serialization, implicit string conversion, pointer-derived
//! representation, variable-width integer encoding, or runtime-dependent
//! framing is permitted to enter the commitment digest.
//!
//! ### State Binding Parameters
//!
//! Where:
//! - `C_receipt` is the commitment contained in the `PersistenceReceipt` capability evidence.
//! - `H_terminal` is the resident cryptographic state hash of the engine at the moment `rearm()` is invoked.
//! - `H_terminal` is **never** reconstructed from persistence evidence.
//! - `Encode_Canonical(artifact)` is the length-prefixed, deterministic byte representation of the persisted terminal artifact.
//!
//! The receipt is valid **only** relative to the exact resident `H_terminal` against which its commitment is recomputed.
//!
//! ---
//!
//! ## Formal Operational Guarantees
//!
//! ### 1. Zero External Trust
//! A compromised storage layer, forged `PersistenceAdapter`, or arbitrary external caller cannot force a state reset by presenting a syntactically valid receipt. External persistence provides bytes and evidence only. Authorization remains resident in the engine because verification is strictly bound to `H_terminal`.
//!
//! ### 2. Payload Identity
//! Any modification to the persisted artifact, including:
//! - a single-bit mutation,
//! - truncation or byte extension,
//! - field substitution, or
//! - non-canonical re-encoding,
//!
//! alters `Encode_Canonical(artifact)` or its resulting commitment and causes instant authorization failure.
//!
//! ### 3. Terminal-State Non-Substitution
//! A receipt bound to terminal state `H_terminal_A` cannot computationally
//! authorize rearm of an engine currently holding terminal state
//! `H_terminal_B`, where:
//!
//! ```text
//! H_terminal_A != H_terminal_B
//! ```
//!
//! The engine independently computes:
//!
//! ```text
//! C_expected_B = H(
//!     VERSION
//!     || DOMAIN_PERSISTENCE_RECEIPT
//!     || H_terminal_B
//!     || Encode_Canonical(artifact)
//! )
//! ```
//!
//! A receipt generated against `H_terminal_A` is rejected unless an adversary
//! can produce a cryptographic collision or second preimage against the selected
//! hash construction.
//!
//! Therefore:
//!
//! ```text
//! C_receipt != C_expected_B => rearm() rejected
//! ```
//!
//! under the assumed collision-resistance and second-preimage resistance of the
//! protocol hash function.
//!
//! ### 4. Epoch Non-Replayability
//! `H_terminal` incorporates the cryptographic execution lineage of its epoch.
//!
//! ```text
//! E1 != E2
//!     => canonical lineage inputs differ
//!     => distinct domain-separated terminal commitments are computed
//!     => cross-epoch substitution requires breaking the cryptographic
//!        security assumptions of H
//! ```
//!
//! A persistence receipt is therefore bound to a specific terminal lineage and
//! cannot become a general-purpose reset credential.
//!
//! ### 5. Failure Atomicity
//! All authorization checks **MUST** complete before the engine mutates its resident state. On any verification failure:
//!
//! ```text
//! rearm(...) -> Err(self)
//! ```
//!
//! The returned engine **MUST** preserve its pre-invocation logical state. In particular, failed verification **MUST NOT**:
//! - transition the state machine,
//! - replace or overwrite `H_terminal`,
//! - zeroize valid resident state,
//! - partially restore persisted state, or
//! - consume authorization evidence.
//!
//! ### 6. Successful Transition
//! Only after complete commitment verification may the terminal state transition to `Idle`. The resulting active state **MUST** derive its new genesis state exclusively from protocol-defined deterministic derivation rules and **never** from unverified persistence bytes.
//!
//! ---
//!
//! ## Architectural Security Boundary
//!
//! ```text
//!                    External Storage / Unverified Host
//!                                    |
//!                      artifact + PersistenceReceipt
//!                                    v
//!                 +--------------------------------------+
//!                 |  Resident Canonical Verification     |
//!                 |                                      |
//!                 |  C_expected = H( VERSION || ... )    |
//!                 +------------------+-------------------+
//!                                    |
//!                              exact equality
//!                                    |
//!                         +----------+----------+
//!                         |                     |
//!                      reject                 accept
//!                         |                     |
//!                      Err(self)         authorized reset
//!                         |                     |
//!                         v                     v
//!                   Retain State               Idle
//! ```
//!
//! > **Core Security Property:**
//! > Possession of persistence evidence is insufficient to authorize rearm.
//! > Rearm authority exists only when independently recomputed evidence binds
//! > exactly to the cryptographic terminal state resident in the engine.
